  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Exact genus-2/3 QQ Cantor results now retain one opaque owned FLINT `(u,v)` pair plus an authoritative immutable primitive row behind a closure-private WeakMap; ordinary public divisors remain lazy, survive prepared-context close/workspace reuse, and materialize only when `uv()` or serialization reconstruction requires polynomials. Public exact equality, hashing, packing, same-parent addition, scalar chaining, memory/cancellation bounds, and reference certificates preserve their contracts. Module-helper rebinding, plausible attribute injection, owner transplant, hash-cache injection, component/resource inspection, closed pair reuse, and overlapping pair loads fail safely. The 10,000-call local receipt measured 0.215 ms per public 257-bit torsion scalar, 0.170 ms per ordinary public nontrivial addition, 0.131 ms per prepared addition, 0.162 ms per chained retained addition, 0.556 ms including forced `(u,v)` materialization, and 0.205 ms including hashing. Public addition is about 5.6x faster than the previous 0.95 ms path, but still honestly misses the old timer-quantized Magma 0.01 ms/call row by about 17x; no new bench-1 comparison was run without authorization.",
    "risks": [
      "Integration must deliberately raise the hyperelliptic-curves-kernels lazy budget from 175000 bytes to at least the measured 177359 bytes; this lane did not hide the architecture:check failure.",
      "Integration must classify exactly three new desktop-only WebAssembly capabilities with the existing exact reference fallback: ffi-resource:flint:fmpq_polynomial_pair, ffi:flint:fmpq_polynomial_workspace_copy_pair_out, and ffi:flint:fmpq_polynomial_workspace_load_pair.",
      "Windows uses the tested exact reference fallback until the generated FLINT rational-polynomial workspace is available there.",
      "The strict public QQ addition <=2x Magma gate remains open; the prior Magma row is only 0.01-second timer-quantized over 1000 calls, so a new same-host acceptance is required after integration."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Apply the package-budget and three WebAssembly capability dispositions in the integration lane, then rerun the complete architecture gate.",
      "After explicit bench-1 authorization, repeat the equal-contract warmed/cold public P+Q and 257-bit scalar receipt against resident Magma.",
      "If the public addition gate remains outside 2x, profile a single source-transparent operation that returns the exact primitive row and opaque pair with fewer runtime crossings; do not move Cantor mathematics into a host adapter."
    ]
  }
